From 0d1c51c0a749e4eb3d7479e43d249a2ee0d938dc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 16:57:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Phase 3: add exit-policy tracker (v0.5.3.24)

Adds the missing exit-management layer the .15/.16 docstrings both flag
as absent: once a paper order is confirmed filled by .18 Reconciliation
(RECONCILED_EXECUTION + position_exists=True), nothing in .12-.19
decides when to close it. This module fills that gap.

- Consumes ONLY .18's reconciliation.json (hash-verified, mirroring the
  same canonical-hash check .23 already does against .19) and the same
  alpaca_1h_closed_bars.csv .12 already reads -- no new market-data
  fetch, no order placement, no fabricated fill/position.
- Reuses aura_exit_policy_backtest.py's simulate_trade() verbatim
  (imported via importlib, matching this repo's existing convention) for
  the actual trailing-stop/take-profit math -- not reimplemented.
- Policy (direction/trailing_stop_pct/take_profit_pct/max_hold_bars) is
  explicit per-symbol via --policy-config, mirroring .23's
  VALIDATED_*_ENTRY_REGIME_LABELS pattern: an open position with no
  matching config entry is reported POLICY_MISSING, never given an
  assumed policy.
- No state is persisted across cycles -- every run replays the full
  history from entry_ts through simulate_trade(), so output can never
  drift from a stored/stale tracker state.
- Adapts simulate_trade()'s backtest-only TIMEOUT branch for live use:
  downgrades a premature TIMEOUT to HOLD when fewer bars have been
  fetched since entry than the policy's own max_hold_bars, since that
  branch can't otherwise tell "ran out of fetched bars" from "policy
  hold window actually elapsed". STOP/TARGET verdicts are trusted
  immediately regardless of window completeness.
- Never places an order itself -- only emits HOLD/EXIT/POLICY_MISSING
  per open symbol for a later step (Phase 5) to act on.
- 20 new tests (tests/test_aura_v05324_exit_policy_tracker.py); full
  suite at 137/137 passing (excluding the 2 pre-existing tests that
  require live Alpaca credentials, unrelated to this change).

